# k3s node self-test
#
# Copy as /boot/firmware/cupcake-selftest.txt on a control plane or a worker. Its contents are ignored; it is deleted
# when the self-test starts, so each copy runs it once, on the next boot.
#
# It only reads, so the node can be used afterwards. It waits up to 15 minutes for k3s to settle, then checks:
#   - setup from cupcake-k3s.txt, problems in cupcake-k3s-error.txt, mDNS
#   - k3s, every node Ready, CoreDNS, Traefik and cert-manager, or a worker's control plane
#   - the preloaded images, and the USB drive when cupcake-storage.txt chose one
#   - on the control plane: cupcake-master, its certificate authority, HTTPS and the HTTP redirect, every instance
#   - Tailscale and the Cloudflare tunnel
#   - board, memory, temperature, throttling, SD card write speed, boot time and failed services
#
# Results are written next to this file:
#   cupcake-selftest-report.txt   summary
#   cupcake-selftest-report.json  full report
#
# The activity LED shows the outcome until the next reboot: a heartbeat for pass, a fast blink for failure.
